bg3le stats: a string pool candidate must have the guid, float and translated pools after it

On top of 0001-0015. find_string_pool took the first array of 256+ entries holding a dice string. On 11 of 655 kept
launches that was the 1512-entry array at -384 from the rarity run (TreasureTables' NextIds by the header), not the real
pool at +32: guid, float and translated pools came up missing, "attributes available" was logged anyway, and FixedString
writes went into the engine's array (arena S5 2026-11-06: Size 1512 -> 1524, no Progressions landed). Over the kept logs
all 1287 good scans have all three pools at +32/+48/+64 from the pool, and all 22 bad scans have none.

- A candidate passes only with those three pools after it (pool_block_holds), using find_value_pools' own checks, moved
  to file scope. The scan goes on past a false match.
- The dice string, its id and the entry it matched go in the log, for a rejected candidate and for the chosen one: why
  the dice test passes on that array is still not explained, and the next false match says.
- Attributes need the string pool: with no candidate the log says so, "attributes unavailable", and reads and writes
  refuse instead of going through a wrong pool.

Test: tools/test_bg3le_stats_pool.py.

